! Silicon, two atoms, one k-point: the reference case for the single-core
! comparison against Quantum ESPRESSO (tools/compare_qe.py).
!
! Identical to test-suite/pw_scf/scf.in except that the two-point k-set is cut
! to the first point alone. One k-point removes the k-parallel axis from both
! codes, so what is compared is the cost of a single Hamiltonian solve, a single
! density, and the potential -- not how well either code batches over k.
!
! conv_thr is tightened well past what either code needs so that both run to the
! same fixed point: the comparison then reports a cost per iteration that means
! the same thing on both sides, and the two total energies agreeing to 1e-8 Ry
! doubles as a correctness check on every optimisation.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1) =10.20,
    nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=12.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS
  1
   0.250000  0.250000  0.250000   1.00
